Qapla' Project — training corpus
================================

The file `klingon.txt` in this directory is derived from:

    klingon-assistant-data (the data behind the boQwI' dictionary)
    https://github.com/De7vID/klingon-assistant-data
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

What we changed: we extracted the example sentences from that dataset, dropped
any sentence containing characters outside the romanised Klingon orthography
plus basic punctuation, dropped single-word entries, deduplicated, and repeated
the remainder 15 times so a very small char-level model has enough to chew on.
`build_corpus.py` in this directory performs exactly those steps and will
regenerate the file from the original source.

A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is included at the root of this
repository (LICENSE).

A note on what is NOT here
--------------------------

The training run documented in the README used this corpus plus a supplementary
list of frequent Klingon words drawn from a third-party corpus site whose
licensing we could not verify. We are not redistributing that part. The corpus
published here is therefore the clean, Apache 2.0 subset — same character
vocabulary, about 81% of the bytes. Expect results in the same range, not an
exact byte-for-byte reproduction of our numbers.

